==Battleground==
*4 [[Miz Devil]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 6.67~10 seconds<sup>200f~300f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Ginger Snache]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 23.33~30 seconds<sup>700f~900f</sup>.
*1 [[Celeboodle]] spawns after 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Li'l Nyandam (Enemy)|Li'l Nyandam]] spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[Miz Devil]]s spawn, delay 13.33~20 seconds<sup>400f~600f</sup>.
**5 [[Celeboodle]]s spawn, delay 53.33~60 seconds<sup>1,600f~1,800f</sup>.
**2 [[Rain D.|Rain Ds]] spawn, delay 120 seconds<sup>3,600f</sup>.
**3 [[Aku Gory|Aku Gories]] spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 66.67~73.33 seconds<sup>2,000f~2,200f</sup>.
**1 [[Midnite D.]] spawns after 60 seconds<sup>1,800f</sup>.

==Strategy==
After almost 20 Zero Legends subchapters later, Li'l Nyandam finally gets to shine. Unfortunately, this stage, just like [[Saint Red Fox]], is incredibly easy and will require next to no effort to clear. While Li'l Nyandam himself is buffed to 300%, giving him stats similar to a normal Nyandam, his support doesn't do anything to help him given that this stage is entirely on base hit. At the start of the stage, use the Miz Devils to build up a small stack of [[Apple Cat (Super Rare Cat)|iCats]], [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cats]], and meatshields. Have Courier or someone else hit the base, to which you are greeted by a Rain D. and Li'l Nyandam himself. When this happens, send out your trusty [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] to beat up Rain D., and he should be knocked back enough to where he'll just start getting juggled by your Couriers and Bahamut. As for Li'l Nyandam himself, he won't be doing much in his extremely small lifespan given your iCats constantly Freezing him. The Aku Gory that appears next will meet a similar fate of getting juggled, and once Li'l Nyandam dies you should be able to beat the stage before Midnite D. can even spawn.

==Trivia==
*Fudge Mausoleum's Japanese name, Hin'yari Choko Reibyō (ひんやりチョコ霊廟, "Chilly Choco Mausoleum"), contains a pun on チョコレート ''chokorēto'' (chocolate) and 霊廟 ''reibyō'' (mausoleum).
*[[Li'l Nyandam (Enemy)|Li'l Nyandam]] appearing in Fudge Mausoleum is likely a reference to his love of sweets.

